{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_544a87d6ad4d499ebbdc8bc99cd6dff0","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_afb163250a804e714901a4165b99e9bac622ef5881646d1fa92407fc0cfe2389","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"qcri/codebadger@857adcabe386 snapshot 4467dca7c5129a6c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_931a819511e478dff9335bdd6a18d02066609ca8cffa247f9f89856ac091363e"],"source_ids":["src_ef788ac249965ceb908dded43a823db8"],"text":"It accepts a Git repository, local path, or pasted snippet, builds a CPG, and exposes it over MCP for CPGQL queries, taint tracing, slicing, and vulnerability hunting.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_544a87d6ad4d499ebbdc8bc99cd6dff0"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_544a87d6ad4d499ebbdc8bc99cd6dff0","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b70b2702076dc089762bdc197e643d4e093417d6d2ed28ad5e42295b64c90b97","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"qcri/codebadger@857adcabe386 snapshot 4467dca7c5129a6c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2093e3099d195a2b7582e1a1aea6cd41c450b9b2d14e1349d18afe1c37da3710"],"source_ids":["src_0ef6494d1cdb550fb70fc65f0a6782ba"],"text":"Postgres stores catalog, tool cache, findings, and the durable job queue; Redis holds cross-process query locks and the pool ledger, and the server refuses to boot if either is unreachable.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_544a87d6ad4d499ebbdc8bc99cd6dff0"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_544a87d6ad4d499ebbdc8bc99cd6dff0","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c4d3ec1a1eff10baba78763332f400021c9f4b3d26516b39a80d40ffed4cf37f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"qcri/codebadger@857adcabe386 snapshot 4467dca7c5129a6c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_52b7d42ae79217ce43b0f47743528a8977616e20c3459f380ab8722b72fef1d7"],"source_ids":["src_0ef6494d1cdb550fb70fc65f0a6782ba"],"text":"CPGs are disk-cached by content hash; sleeping servers cost no RAM and wake by re-importing the cached .bin on the next query.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_544a87d6ad4d499ebbdc8bc99cd6dff0"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_544a87d6ad4d499ebbdc8bc99cd6dff0","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cad58bb0f79f261bb375a9cf2b3748f801aa7ed68c4451b0a78201a56c2e41a1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"qcri/codebadger@857adcabe386 snapshot 4467dca7c5129a6c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_593cf1cf4189b7a77a10cbc0cd6e57911e14f4e64ac7c46189fdb510c05eb7d3","slc_93a7f973444614b36fdd824f512f5a295eeb2c13b79905b978e8f78137314620"],"source_ids":["src_0ef6494d1cdb550fb70fc65f0a6782ba"],"text":"A GET /health endpoint probes joern, postgres, redis, docker, and cpg_queue concurrently, returning up/partial/down with HTTP 200/503 for orchestrators.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_544a87d6ad4d499ebbdc8bc99cd6dff0"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_544a87d6ad4d499ebbdc8bc99cd6dff0","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d5b7cab0ede4e71c693091319690d6b5c4a003541a2e1dd4a0d40724360426a9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"qcri/codebadger@857adcabe386 snapshot 4467dca7c5129a6c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5328db95ea749eefe27b307a818e7236649804cb2cd8a2c30fdae4dce2772bb2","slc_6c950d604c73e42ea6c2cd0a6b6575e8c9c754631eaa1684d2f17a34f17e4af6"],"source_ids":["src_0ef6494d1cdb550fb70fc65f0a6782ba"],"text":"Admission is governed by a memory budget rather than a fixed server count: heap tiers derive from CPG size, with LRU eviction, an RSS backstop, and an idle-TTL reaper (default 600s).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_544a87d6ad4d499ebbdc8bc99cd6dff0"}
